15.500 TL
("Excellent! We shall then look thoroughly into the affair. Of course there is only one) Tj
T*
(feasible explanation. You have been brought there to personate someone, and the real) Tj
T*
(person is imprisoned in this chamber. That is obvious. As to who this prisoner is, I have) Tj
T*
(no doubt that it is the daughter, Miss Alice Rucastle, if I remember right, who was said) Tj
T*
(to have gone to America. You were chosen, doubtless, as resembling her in height, figure,) Tj
T*
(and the colour of your hair. Hers had been cut off, very possibly in some illness through) Tj
T*
(which she has passed, and so, of course, yours had to be sacrificed also. By a curious) Tj
T*
(chance you came upon her tresses. The man in the road was undoubtedly some friend of) Tj
T*
(hers--possibly her _fiancé_--and no doubt, as you wore the girl's dress and were so like) Tj
T*
(her, he was convinced from your laughter, whenever he saw you, and afterwards from your) Tj
T*
(gesture, that Miss Rucastle was perfectly happy, and that she no longer desired his) Tj
T*
(attentions. The dog is let loose at night to prevent him from endeavouring to communicate) Tj
T*
(with her. So much is fairly clear. The most serious point in the case is the disposition) Tj
T*
(of the child.") Tj
